
Healthy Hunger – Project Scope & Requirements
4 Oct 2026 · @Lay Patel
One web app for Healthy Hunger: a public landing page, a QR menu where customers order for their table or for parcel, and a staff dashboard that takes those orders and keeps customer records.
Goals
Version 1 is done when a customer can scan a table QR, browse the menu, place an order, and see it land on the staff screen within seconds.
1. Landing page that introduces the café, its promise (100% veg, protein-forward), location, hours and contact.
2. QR menu that opens on a phone in under 2 seconds and shows each item's veg mark, description, protein, calories and ₹ price.
3. Ordering for two types: dine-in (linked to a table number) and parcel (takeaway).
4. Admin dashboard where staff see new orders live, move them through statuses, and mark them paid.
5. Customer records built from orders: name, phone, email, visit count and spend.
6. Menu control so the owner can change prices, mark items sold out and add new items without a developer.
At a glance
Customers and staff use the same Next.js app; the menu, orders and customer records all live in one PostgreSQL database.
