Order status flow
1. New – placed by the customer; the dashboard plays a sound
2. Accepted – staff confirm it (and confirm the customer is at the table or will collect)
3. Preparing
4. Ready – for parcel, the customer is told it is ready to collect
5. Served / Picked up
6. Paid – cash, UPI or card recorded
An order can be Cancelled from New, Accepted or Preparing, with a reason. After placing, the customer sees an order number and a live status page at /order/{id}.
Guard rails against fake orders: one open order per table at a time (staff can add items to it), a short limit on orders per phone number per hour, and staff must accept before the kitchen starts.
