Customer data
A customer record is created or updated automatically each time an order is placed with a phone number. Only the owner can see the full customer list.
• Stored: name, phone, email, first visit, last visit, number of orders, total spend, favourite items, staff notes, marketing consent (yes / no and the date given)
• Consent: the order form says why we collect phone and email (to manage the order and contact the customer about it). Offers by WhatsApp, SMS or email go only to customers who ticked the consent box.
• Privacy: a short privacy note linked in the footer and the order form. The owner can delete a customer's data on request. This follows the basic ideas of India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (consent, a clear purpose, deletion on request); have it checked before launch.
• Security: phone numbers are partly hidden in staff views (98xxxxxx21); full numbers and CSV export are for the owner only.
