The stack, piece by piece
• Framework: Next.js (App Router) with TypeScript. The landing page and menu are pre-rendered for speed and refreshed when the owner edits the menu.
• Server logic: Server Actions and Route Handlers for orders, status changes and admin actions; Zod to check every form.
• Database: PostgreSQL with Prisma (schema and migrations in one place).
• Login: Auth.js with username / password for staff and owner, and role checks on every admin page and action.
• Live orders: start with the dashboard asking for new orders every 5 seconds (simple and reliable); move to Server-Sent Events later if needed.
• UI: Tailwind CSS with the palette as design tokens, plus shadcn/ui for dashboard tables, dialogs and forms.
• Images: stored on the server (or Cloudflare R2) and served through the Next.js image optimiser.
• Hosting: one Linux VPS in an India region (Mumbai) running Docker Compose: Next.js + PostgreSQL + Caddy for automatic HTTPS, with a daily database backup job. Vercel + a hosted Postgres is the no-server-admin alternative.
When to add Django later: if the café grows to several branches, gets a mobile app, or needs heavy data work, a Django + Django REST Framework API can be added behind the same Next.js frontend. Starting with a clean database schema keeps that move simple.
Open questions
[ ] QR codes: the printed cards point to the current artifact link. The new site needs a domain and one QR per table, so the cards will be reprinted. How many tables?
[ ] Domain name: e.g. healthyhunger.in. Which one, and who buys it?
[ ] Dine-in details: should dine-in customers have to give a phone number, or only parcel customers?
[ ] Payment: counter only (cash / UPI) for v1, or online UPI from day one?
[ ] Tax: is the café GST-registered? Should bills show GST?
[ ] Bills and KOT: is there a thermal printer at the counter or in the kitchen?
[ ] Brand colours: fully replace leaf green and turmeric yellow with the wall palette, or keep one as a small accent?
[ ] Pending café details: address, phone, WhatsApp, Instagram handle, final hours, final prices.
[ ] Staff: how many staff logins at launch?
[ ] Opening date: sets the deadline for phases 1–5.
